# deploy
NODE_ENV - runtime mode of the wallet gateway process, production on the platform
PORT - port the wallet gateway listens on behind the platform proxy
ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's node key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's backup key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT - platform secret holding this attestor's TLS certificate, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's TLS private key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_CA - platform secret holding the CA bundle for peers and the gateway, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE
ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA - platform secret holding the operator CA bundle, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA_FILE
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LISTEN - socket address the shared endpoint listens on, defaulting to all interfaces on port 9443
LAYERX_GATEWAY_NETWORK_ID - network identifier the shared endpoint expects from its kernel backends, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROTOCOL_NETWORK_ID - numeric protocol network identifier of the kernel, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LXP_WIRE_VERSION - LXP wire version the shared endpoint speaks
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDEMPOTENCY_SECONDS - retention of idempotency records in seconds
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CAPABILITIES_TTL_SECONDS - cache lifetime of the capabilities answer in seconds
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LISTENER - listener mode of the shared endpoint: tls, the default, terminates TLS with the certificate and key; plain serves plain HTTP behind the platform proxy and refuses both of them
LAYERX_GATEWAY_TLS_CERT_DER - path to the shared endpoint's DER server certificate
LAYERX_GATEWAY_TLS_KEY_DER - path to the shared endpoint's DER PKCS8 server key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_OUTBOUND_CA_DER - path to the DER CA that authenticates the endpoint's upstream services
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PKCS12 - path to the PKCS12 client identity the endpoint presents upstream
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PASSWORD_FILE - path to the password of the PKCS12 client identity
LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_URL - agent boundary base URL, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_TOKEN_FILE - path to the agent boundary bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_URL - receipt authority base URL, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the receipt authority bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_URL - identity service base URL, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the identity service bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN_FILE - path to the identity provisioning token used by registration
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_URL - program registry base URL, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the program registry bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_CORE_URL - public core read base URL, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PAXEER_RPC_URL - chain RPC base URL for eth_ relay, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_INDEXER_URL - indexer base URL for unified history, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_URL - faucet service base URL, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE - path to the faucet service token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_URL - Redis URL of the endpoint's shared store, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_USERNAME_FILE - path to the Redis username
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_PASSWORD_FILE - path to the Redis password
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE - path to the trusted sequencer public key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_ID_FILE - path to the trusted sequencer identifier
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH_FILE - path to the first batch the sequencer authorisation covers
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH_FILE - path to the last batch the sequencer authorisation covers
LAYERX_GATEWAY_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY_FILE - path to the 64-hex key provisioning key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_MODULE_REGISTRY_FILE - path to the module registry JSON document
ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_OUTBOUND_CA_DER
ENDPOINT_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PKCS12 - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PKCS12
ENDPOINT_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PASSWORD - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PASSWORD_FILE
ENDPOINT_COMPONENT_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_AUTHORITY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_IDENTITY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_REDIS_USERNAME - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_USERNAME_FILE
ENDPOINT_REDIS_PASSWORD - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_PASSWORD_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_ID - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_ID_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH_FILE
ENDPOINT_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY_FILE
ENDPOINT_MODULE_REGISTRY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_MODULE_REGISTRY_FILE
# attestor
ATTESTOR_NODE_ID - identifier of this attestor node within the participant set
ATTESTOR_REGION - region label this node reports in health
ATTESTOR_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the attestor API listens on
ATTESTOR_PEER_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the peer transport listens on
ATTESTOR_PEERS - comma-separated id=host:port list of the other attestor nodes
ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY_FILE - path to the node key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts the share store
ATTESTOR_DATA_DIR - directory holding the encrypted share store
ATTESTOR_CEREMONY - true enables keys.import for the operator during a ceremony window
ATTESTOR_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id every decoded transaction is pinned to
ATTESTOR_JWKS_URL - identity provider JWKS endpoint used to verify user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_ISSUER - expected issuer of user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_AUDIENCE - expected audience of user tokens
ATTESTOR_POLICY_FILE - path to the default signing policy
ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE - path to this node's TLS certificate
ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE - path to this node's TLS private key
ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates peers and the gateway
ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates the operator identity
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY_FILE - path to the key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts store snapshots
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_DIR - directory where encrypted store snapshots are written
ATTESTOR_RPC_URL - chain RPC endpoint used to read nonces and binding state

# gateway
NODE_ENV - runtime mode of the gateway: development, test or production
PORT - TCP port the gateway HTTP server listens on
LOG_LEVEL - gateway log verbosity
CORS_ORIGINS - comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the gateway, with single-level wildcard subdomains
SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL whose published JWKS verifies user access tokens
DATABASE_URL - connection string of the gateway's wallet database
DATABASE_POOL_MAX - maximum connections in the gateway's database pool
WALLET_MASTER_KEY - base64 32-byte key that encrypts legacy wallet key envelopes at rest
WALLET_MASTER_KEY_VERSION - version number of the active wallet master key
HYPERPAXEER_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id the gateway signs for
HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL - EVM JSON-RPC endpoint used for reads and broadcasts
HYPERPAXEER_EXPLORER_URL - block explorer base URL returned to clients for transaction links
POLICY_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - per-transaction native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - rolling daily native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests allowed per wallet per minute
FUNDED_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY - treasury signing key of the funded lane, disabled when unset
FUNDED_USDL_ADDRESS - USDL token contract used as funded-lane collateral
FUNDED_USDL_DECIMALS - decimals of the USDL token
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_THRESHOLD_WEI - native balance below which a funded wallet is topped up
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_AMOUNT_WEI - native amount sent per funded-wallet top-up
FUNDED_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the funded drawdown evaluator
PAXSCAN_API_URL - explorer API base used to value funded wallets
PAXSCAN_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one explorer API request
PAXSCAN_CACHE_TTL_MS - lifetime of cached explorer valuations
FUNDED_BALANCE_READ_QUORUM - number of RPC reads sampled per funded balance read
FUNDED_DAILY_RESET_UTC_HOUR - UTC hour at which the funded daily drawdown window resets
API_WORKERS - number of gateway worker processes
AGENT_JWT_SECRET - HS256 secret that signs gateway-minted agent tokens, agent lane disabled when unset
AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent token
AGENT_CHALLENGE_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent authentication challenge
AGENT_DEFAULT_FROZEN - whether a newly seen agent principal starts frozen
AGENT_DEFAULT_MODE - initial mode of a newly seen agent principal
AGENT_BIND_OWNER_FROM_DID - whether an agent is bound to the owner named in its DID label
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - default per-transaction native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - default rolling daily native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - default signing requests per agent per minute
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_APPROVE_WEI - default cap on ERC-20 approval amounts for agent wallets
LAYERX_VAULT_ADDRESS - LayerX custody vault contract targeted by agent deposit actions
LAYER_X_DB_URI - read-only connection string of the LayerX sequencer database
ACTION_CONFIRMATIONS - block confirmations before an agent action transaction is final
ACTION_RECEIPT_TIMEOUT_MS - maximum wait for one agent action receipt
ACTION_WORKER_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the agent action worker
ACTION_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS - sweep interval of the agent action reconciler
ACTION_FEE_BUMP_PERCENT - fee increase applied when replacing a stuck agent action transaction
LAYERX_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS - interval of the LayerX mirror sync worker
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_WALLET_API - wallet gateway base URL used by the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY - Supabase publishable key used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL - sign-in callback URL of the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL - public origin of the demo used for page metadata
# gateway
ATTESTOR_ENDPOINTS - comma-separated https base URLs of the five attestor nodes the gateway signs through
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_CERT_FILE - path to the gateway's mutual TLS client certificate presented to the attestors
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_KEY_FILE - path to the private key of the gateway's mutual TLS client certificate
ATTESTOR_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates the attestor nodes
ATTESTOR_QUORUM - number of healthy attestors a signing session needs, defaulting to 3
ATTESTOR_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS - interval between attestor health probes in milliseconds, defaulting to 5000
ATTESTOR_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one attestor request in milliseconds, defaulting to 15000
RPC_URLS - comma-separated chain RPC URLs of the gateway's RPC pool, defaulting to the sixteen public mainnet hosts
RPC_LAG_THRESHOLD_BLOCKS - blocks an RPC endpoint may trail the best head before it leaves the pool, defaulting to 20
RPC_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS - interval between RPC pool health checks in milliseconds, defaulting to 5000
RPC_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one RPC request in milliseconds, defaulting to 8000
RATE_LIMIT_CLIENT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests one bearer subject may make per minute, defaulting to 120
RATE_LIMIT_ACCOUNT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests one wallet account may receive per minute, defaulting to 60
AGENT_JWT_SECRET - platform secret signing the read-scoped agent token; unset disables the agent lane
AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of the read-scoped agent token in seconds
AGENT_CHALLENGE_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent authentication challenge in seconds
AGENT_REQUEST_MAX_TTL_SECONDS - furthest expiry in seconds an agent request signature or claim counter-signature may carry, default 300
LAYERX_USDL_ADDRESS - USDL token address used by the kernel deposit action
LAYERX_USDL_DECIMALS - USDL token decimals used when the token does not report them
FUNDED_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY - removed with the funded lane; must not be set anywhere
FUNDED_USDL_ADDRESS - removed; replaced by LAYERX_USDL_ADDRESS
FUNDED_USDL_DECIMALS - removed; replaced by LAYERX_USDL_DECIMALS
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_THRESHOLD_WEI - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_AMOUNT_WEI - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL_MS - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_BALANCE_READ_QUORUM - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_DAILY_RESET_UTC_HOUR - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_API_URL - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_TIMEOUT_MS - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_CACHE_TTL_MS - removed with the funded lane
AGENT_BIND_OWNER_FROM_DID - removed; an owner is recorded only through the authenticated claim route
